the great Jedi are a group of force  users who chose to distance themselves  from the Jedi Order  due to their conflicting beliefs in how  the force should be used in order for us  to understand why they chose to do this  so we first have to understand the force  and those who harness its power in the  Star Wars universe when we think of the  force we think of the Jedi and the Sith  the light and the dark side there are  two distinct sites who have conflicting  views on how the force should be used  the Jedi Order is structured much like a  religion with clear beliefs and rules on  how the force should be used that are  strictly adhered to they focus on  self-discipline selflessness and inner  peace as their path to the force and  they consider themselves to be the  guardians of peace within a galaxy on  the other side of course you have the  Sith a common misconception of the Sith  that the movies do not help to dispel is  that the syph are inherently evil  there is no denying that the Sith crave  power but whether the Jedi consider  emotions to be a path down the dark side  this if embraced their emotion these  emotions can be anger and hatred but  they can also be joy or love one of the  main reasons the Sith are depicted as  becoming evil is because they are  blinded or corrupted by their passion  and emotions the grey Jedi as their name  may suggest do not see the force in the  black and white terms of the Jedi and  the Sith do the gray Jedi see the force  as a spectrum of power with light and  dark philosophies on either side they  stand firmly in the middle believe in  that the only true way to master the  force is with a balance of light and  dark  a Jedi who disagreed with a council may  have been seen as a great Jedi and  despite this never being mentioned in  the Canon universe there are those who  consider qui-gon jinn to be a great Jedi  because of his many disagreements with  the Jedi Council we do see obi-wan  mention that if he's master would just  follow the code then he would already be  on the council alluding to the  possibility that Jin did not follow the  Jedi Code as closely as others  it was Jin's independence from the  council as well as his former master  Dooku joining a dark side that made them  wary of Jin possibly suspecting him of  being a great Jedi one could argue that  a line of great Jedi were indirectly  created through the teachings of qui-gon  jinn even after his death the series of  Padawans that followed in his footsteps  including obi-wan Kenobi Anakin and Luke  Skywalker all had severe disagreements  with the Jedi Code and more often seen  as maverick Jedi's potentially even gray  Jedi's if we take a look at ahsoka tano  from Star Wars rebels in the Clone Wars  she does fit into this line of potential  great Jedi left behind by qui-gon jinn  she was Padawan - anakin skywalker for a  short period and displayed behavior that  we've come to expect from a great Jedi  routinely disobeying the orders of the  council much like her master at the time  she was very aggressive and eager for  battle willing to use means that the  Jedi Council would not approve of to get  what she wanted in this case the term  great Jedi does not necessarily refer to  a Jedi who embraces a dark side but one  who doesn't fully comply with the  teachings of the Jedi Order such as not  being able to have a family or study and  learn the dark side of the force  [Music]  one of the most well known examples of a  great Jedi in the extended universe was  Joe Lee bindle Bindo was inducted into  the Jedi Order and trained in the ways  of the force at the Khorasan Jedi Temple  as a Padawan  Binda was considered to be reckless and  often ignored the word of the High  Council when he felt they were wrong he  eventually married a force sensitive  woman named Naima although marriage was  frowned upon by the Jedi Council Bindo  decided that he would train her himself  despite the council being against the  idea and the fact that he was still a  Padawan in this case the Jedi counsels  advice would appear to be correct as  bindas wife returned to the dark side  during the wall of Exar Kun she  attempted to turn Bindo but he rejected  her proposal which led to a lightsaber  duel between the two despite Binda being  victorious he could not kill his wife  and he let her go his wife would go on  to kill many Jedi before she was  eventually struck down in battle after  these events the Jedi Council did not  punish bin though they had hoped he'd  learned his lesson even offering to make  him a Jedi Knight at this point in time  Bindo had lost all faith in the council  and declined their offer going into  exile and living as a hermit on Kashyyyk  where he would fight alongside the  Wookiees and help them protect their  land against poachers Binda would  eventually come across one of the most  notorious Jedi in the extended universe  reven he chose to accompany Riven and  aid him in his victory of a Darth Malak  Bindo was heralded for his actions but  it wasn't long after he faded from the  public eye and disappeared forever  the great order believed in a balance of  all things not just the force alone  unlike the Jedi and Sith they chose to  watch over the Galactic Affairs without  intervening unless they deemed it truly  necessary they believed the force did  have two sides but neither was  inherently good or evil it was the  intention of the user that would  determine if the action was good or bad  the great Jedi were capable of using  dark side powers without falling victim  to its corruption a feat that the Jedi  believed to be impossible they even  taught that the great Jedi were unaware  of their own corruption the definition  of a great Jedi may confuse some as over  the years it has changed it could refer  to a Jedi who chooses not to associate  themselves with the Jedi Order or the  Sith in some cases it refers to someone  who disagrees with some of the teachings  of the Jedi Order and in others it  refers to those who have left the order  completely the Star Wars movie universe  has always been black or white with a  clear struggle between good and evil but  could we be seen in a shade of grey in  the last Jedi what about you guys  do you like the grey today do you even  think they should exist in a universe I  look forward to hearing from you in the  comments below as always I've been your  host mythology and fiction explained
 

